# Git, deps, refactoring, compatibility

## Git

- Focused commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `chore:` — not “update stuff”.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, `node_modules`, dumps, or build artifacts.

## Dependencies

- Prefer existing code; add packages only when justified and maintained.

## Refactoring

- Understand architecture first; no drive-by rewrites.
- Preserve behavior unless the task requires change.
- Match existing sound conventions before inventing new ones.

## API compatibility

- Prefer backward-compatible changes; version `/v1` when breaking.
- Do not silently rename/remove response fields.

## Report format (when finishing tasks)

```text
Implemented: ...
Files changed: ...
API changes: ...
Database changes: ...
Validation: TypeScript / Lint / Tests (only if actually run)
Notes: ...
```
